---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import SectionHead from '@/components/SectionHead.astro';
import Disclosure from '@/components/Disclosure.astro';
import DonateBand from '@/components/DonateBand.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/Icon.astro';
import Button from '@/components/Button.astro';
import { awarenessTopics } from '@/data/programmes';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Awareness & Screening"
  description="Hepatitis B and C screening with VFAHT Pakistan, breast and cervical cancer, dengue, thalassemia, diabetes, hypertension and more — RAVISH's awareness and screening programme."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Screening & public education"
    title="Finding what nobody has looked for yet"
    lead="Screening is the cheapest useful thing a medical camp does, and the least visible. Nobody arrives grateful for a blood pressure reading. It is still the reading that changes the most outcomes."
  />

  <!-- hepatitis, the flagship -->
  <section class="band-paper band" aria-labelledby="hepatitis-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr] lg:gap-16">
        <div>
          <SectionHead
            id="hepatitis-title"
            eyebrow="The largest programme"
            title="Hepatitis B and C"
          />

          <div class="mt-9 flex flex-col gap-5">
            <p class="measure text-body text-ash">
              Hepatitis screening with <strong class="font-semibold">VFAHT Pakistan</strong> is the most
              frequently repeated campaign in the RAVISH archive, and VFAHT is the second most frequent
              partner overall. The first joint screening ran on 31 October 2024. It has run many times
              since, in several cities.
            </p>
            <p class="measure text-body text-ash">
              The reason is scale. Pakistan carries close to a fifth of the global hepatitis C burden.
              Around ten million people are diagnosed with hepatitis C worldwide each year, and another
              five million with hepatitis B. Both can sit for a decade behind symptoms mild enough to
              dismiss — occasional abdominal pain, a loss of appetite — and then present as cirrhosis or
              hepatocellular carcinoma.
            </p>
            <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-crimson/25 pl-6">
              <p class="measure text-body text-ash italic">
                “She had been diagnosed with hepatitis C almost ten years earlier, but she never realised
                how destructive the disease could become. She had occasional abdominal pain and a loss of
                appetite, symptoms that many of us would easily dismiss.”
              </p>
              <footer class="mt-3 text-caption text-muted">
                RAVISH FMC, World Hepatitis Day, July 2026
              </footer>
            </blockquote>
            <p class="measure text-body text-ash">
              A screening camp cannot cure any of that. What it can do is find it early enough that
              treatment is still cheap and still works, and tell a family that the vaccine for hepatitis
              B exists and is free at the government facility down the road.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
          <div class="card p-7" data-reveal="rise">
            <span class="card-edge" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <p class="eyebrow text-crimson">Screened at every camp</p>
            <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3.5">
              {
                ['Blood pressure', 'Blood glucose', 'BMI'].map((item) => (
                  <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body text-ash">
                    <Icon name="check" size={18} class="shrink-0 text-ember" />
                    {item}
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-5 text-small leading-relaxed text-muted">
              Not only for patients who mention a symptom. For everyone who comes through registration —
              which is the whole point, because the people who need it most are the ones who did not come
              in about it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-7" data-reveal="rise" style="--reveal-delay:90">
            <span class="card-edge" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <p class="eyebrow text-crimson">And then?</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-small leading-relaxed text-ash">
              A high reading is only useful if something follows it. Since September 2025 that something
              is the RAVISH Clinic — free, weekly, and in the neighbourhood.
            </p>
            <Button href="/clinic" variant="quiet" icon="arrowRight" class="mt-5">The clinic</Button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- all topics -->
  <section class="band-paper-deep band" aria-labelledby="topics-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHead
        id="topics-title"
        eyebrow={`${awarenessTopics.length} campaign topics`}
        title="Everything the awareness programme covers"
        lead="Some are year-round. Some are seasonal — dengue with the monsoon, smog in the Lahore winter, heatstroke in June. Some follow the international health calendar, like Pink October."
      />

      <div class="mt-12">
        <Disclosure
          peek="24rem"
          moreLabel="Show every topic"
          lessLabel="Show fewer"
          count={`${awarenessTopics.length} topics`}
          veil="paper-deep"
        >
          <ul class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
            {
              awarenessTopics.map((topic, i) => (
                <li
                  class="card flex flex-col p-6"
                  data-reveal="rise"
                  style={`--reveal-delay:${Math.min(i, 8) * 45}`}
                >
                  <span class="card-edge" aria-hidden="true" />
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                    <h3 class="text-body font-semibold text-ash">{topic.name}</h3>
                    {topic.scale === 'largest' && <span class="tag shrink-0">Largest</span>}
                  </div>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-small leading-relaxed text-muted">{topic.note}</p>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </Disclosure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- how a campaign runs -->
  <section class="band-paper band" aria-labelledby="how-campaign-title">
    <div class="shell-narrow">
      <SectionHead
        id="how-campaign-title"
        eyebrow="How a campaign runs"
        title="Talks, pamphlets, and a table in the right place"
      />

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-6">
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed text-ash">
          RAVISH promotes preventive healthcare through awareness campaigns on dengue, TB, hepatitis,
          cancers, menstrual hygiene, obesity and monsoon-related risks. Activities include talks,
          pamphlets, and community engagement in hospitals, colleges and public spaces.
        </p>
        <p class="text-caption text-muted">RAVISH, IMPACT 2025</p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed text-ash">
          The pamphlets are in Urdu. That sounds like a small detail and it is the difference between
          advice a patient hears once and advice a patient can show to the person who actually cooks the
          food or buys the cigarettes.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed text-ash">
          Campaigns run alongside online sessions too — a World Hepatitis Day seminar, a menstrual health
          talk in a girls’ school — because the audience that needs the information is not always the
          audience that comes to a camp.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Button href="/get-involved/volunteer" icon="arrowRight">Help run a campaign</Button>
        <Button href="/what-we-do/education" variant="outline">Education & webinars</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <DonateBand compact />
</BaseLayout>
